ian","Polish","Portuguese - Portugal","Portuguese - Brazil","Romanian","Russian","Simplified Chinese","Swedish","Thai","Traditional Chinese","Turkish","Ukrainian","Indonesian","Spanish - Latin America","Vietnamese"],"min":[["OS","Windows XP SP2+"],["Processor","SSE2 instruction set support"],["Memory","1024 MB RAM"],["Graphics","DX9 (shader model 3.0) or DX11 with feature level 9.3 capabilities"],["Storage","2 GB available space"]],"rec":[],"deck":3,"blurb":"Old Man's Journey is a puzzle adventure in which an elderly man sets out on a trip after receiving a letter. As he travels through hand-painted landscapes of hills, villages and coastlines, you help him by reshaping the scenery, pulling and pushing hills so that the layers line up and create a path for him to walk. Along the way, memories from his past reveal the story of his life.\n\nIt is a single-player game that takes a couple of hours to complete, with a slow, gentle pace and no fail states. There is no spoken dialogue; the story is told through pictures. Old Man's Journey suits players who want a short, reflective game with a lovely art style."}}